WEBVTT

00:01.500 --> 00:12.500
Zhu Yuanzhi led troops in a night raid on the Wunu East Camp. However, the east was where the enemy's main force lay. After brief chaos, Shi Lang led iron cavalry to completely surround and annihilate the Xuan troops.

00:13.000 --> 00:26.500
The following day, Shi Lang ordered the severed heads of Zhu Yuanzhi and others displayed before the battle lines. This crushing blow caused morale inside the city to plummet. After less than two days of resistance, Yiyang fell, and you were escorted to the western front to be held as a hostage.
